ity of pure (<bold>a</bold>) CO<sub>2</sub>, (<bold>b</bold>) CH<sub>4</sub>, (<bold>c</bold>) O<sub>2</sub>, and (<bold>d</bold>) N<sub>2</sub>, in the polyimide-based membrane from the UBE UMS-A2 module. Points represent experimental data, and lines represent DMS model predictions (obtained by minimizing the squared solubility differences).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="molecules-30-04524-g004.jpg"><?image-name molecules-30-04524-g004.jpg?><?image-size 88290?><?image-md5 9bbd68faab045ad5496b2a85cff891df?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 2911?><?image-original-width 4207?><?image-scaled-height 529?><?image-scaled-width 764?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a91b/12693044/9bbd68faab04/molecules-30-04524-g004.jpg?><?thumb-name molecules-30-04524-g004.gif?><?thumb-size 6316?><?thumb-md5 5017c03c6f040fd1f8d67c7a5e2f1499?><?thumb-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?thumb-scaled-height 80?><?thumb-scaled-width 115?><?thumb-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a91b/12693044/5017c03c6f04/molecules-30-04524-g004.gif?></graphic></fig><fig position="float" id="molecules-30-04524-f005" orientation="portrait"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Comparison of total solubility and FFV share in total solubility of CO<sub>2</sub>, CH<sub>4</sub>, O<sub>2</sub>, and N<sub>2</sub> in the polyimide-based membrane at (<bold>a</bold>) 308 K and (<bold>b</bold>) 328 K for minimized squared solubility differences.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" position="float" orientation="portrait" xlink:href="molecules-30-04524-g005.jpg"><?image-name molecules-30-04524-g005.jpg?><?image-size 61434?><?image-md5 44488e4baea9bfbe39df51261f909e02?><?image-image-server-status LOAD_COMPLETED?><?image-original-height 1436?><?image-original-width 4155?><?image-scaled-height 261?><?image-scaled-width 755?><?image-cloudpmc-urn urn:cdn:blobs/a91b/12693044/44488e4baea9/mol